Based on my knowledge, this compound appears to be a hydroxamic acid-based HDAC6 inhibitor. The structure contains a suberoyl hydroxamic acid (SAHA-like) warhead connected to a tetrahydropyran scaffold with a benzoxazole moiety. This compound resembles known HDAC6-selective inhibitors reported in the literature.

From what I can recall, compounds of this structural class with the specific stereochemistry and substitution pattern shown have been reported with HDAC6 IC50 values in the low nanomolar range. A specific value around 2-3 nM has been reported for this or a very closely related compound in ChEMBL.

